From 6a8b1ac6ac7935b6ad5a7054d47b49f8499434af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CosmosEx Buildroot <4372835+planeturban@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:16:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ce_main_app: image library sources (IMAGELIB_SOURCES),
 per-source list cache, USB serials

Stage 1 of the floppy library work (cosmosex-floppy-library.md, 6.1):

- IMAGELIB_SOURCES replaces the hardcoded IMAGELIST_URL: an ordered,
  comma-separated list of web lists (http/https), share:<path> and
  usb:<serial>:<path> sources; '!' disables an entry in place; %2C for a
  comma in a path; at most 8. Default: the original joo.kie.sk list, so
  nothing changes without the setting. IMAGELIST_URL / IMAGELIB_SOURCE
  from earlier builds are migrated.
- Every web source's list is cached as <IMAGELIST_CACHE_DIR>/<id>.list
  (build-time define, default /ce/app/imagelists). Lists are merged in
  priority order (first source wins for the same image name). A refresh
  keeps the old list until the new one is in, and keeps it if the
  download fails (source "offline"). Missing lists are retried at most
  once a minute.
- The newest list version is written to IMAGELIST_CACHE_DIR/version for
  update.cpp.
- Settings::getStringLong() (no 255-character limit), keyExists(),
  removeKey().
- USB serials from sysfs (usbserial.cpp, no udev needed),
  ImageStorage::listUsbSticks(), findMountForUsbSerial(),
  resolveLocation() for share:/usb: locations.
- Downloads can name their local file (TDownloadRequest.dstFile).
- Game names keep their original case for display (search stays
  case-insensitive).
- Web API: GET/PUT /api/v1/library/sources, POST /api/v1/library/refresh,
  GET /api/v1/library/search (one result per image, with its games,
  source, downloaded or not, slots), GET /api/v1/library/usb, and
  DELETE /api/v1/floppy/<slot> to eject. PUT accepts only
  application/json.

share: and usb: sources are parsed, resolved and shown, but their folders
are scanned from stage 6.2 on.
